# Documentation Standards for Auditability (Full Reference)

For the quick reference applied to every prompt, see `documentation-standards.mdc`. This file contains the full templates, examples, and checklists.

## 1. JSDoc Requirements

**ALL exported functions MUST have complete JSDoc documentation.**

### Required JSDoc Tags

| Tag | Required For | Description |
|-----|-------------|-------------|
| `@description` | All functions | What the function does |
| `@param` | All parameters | Type and purpose of each parameter |
| `@returns` | All non-void | What gets returned |
| `@throws` | Error conditions | What errors can be thrown |
| `@security` | Auth/security code | Security implications |
| `@audit` | Audit-logged functions | What gets logged to audit tables |

### Complete JSDoc Template

```typescript
/**
 * Creates a new task and assigns it to a user within a foundry.
 * @description Creates a task with proper foundry isolation, validates user permissions, and logs the creation to the audit trail.
 * @param {Object} params - Task creation parameters
 * @param {string} params.foundryId - The foundry this task belongs to
 * @param {string} params.title - Task title (max 200 chars)
 * @param {string} params.assigneeId - User ID to assign task to
 * @param {string} [params.description] - Optional task description
 * @returns {Promise<Task>} The created task with generated ID
 * @throws {UnauthorizedError} If user lacks task.create permission
 * @throws {NotFoundError} If foundry or assignee doesn't exist
 * @throws {ValidationError} If title exceeds 200 characters
 * @security Requires authenticated user with foundry membership
 * @audit Logs task_created event with task_id, foundry_id, created_by
 * @example
 * const task = await createTask({ foundryId: 'foundry_123', title: 'Review quarterly report', assigneeId: 'user_456' })
 */
export async function createTask(params: CreateTaskParams): Promise<Task> {
  // AUTH: Verify user has permission to create tasks in this foundry
  await requirePermission(params.foundryId, 'task.create')
  if (params.title.length > 200) throw new ValidationError('Title must be 200 characters or less')
  // ... implementation
}
```

## 2. Security Annotation Comments

| Prefix | Use For |
|--------|---------|
| `// SECURITY:` | Security-sensitive logic |
| `// AUTH:` | Authentication/authorization |
| `// AUDIT:` | Audit logging |
| `// RLS:` | Row-level security notes |
| `// VALIDATION:` | Input validation |
| `// SENSITIVE:` | Handling sensitive data |

## 3. Business Logic Comments

Explain the **WHY**, not the **WHAT**. Reference tickets (e.g. PRODUCT-456, INCIDENT-2024-03-15) when relevant.

## 4. Component Documentation

Components: JSDoc with `@description` and `@example`. Props: each prop documented with `/** ... */`.

## 5. File Headers

Required for: API routes (auth/payments), files > 200 lines, security-critical logic, migrations. Include @file, @description, @dependencies, @security, @related, @audit as applicable.

## 6. What NOT to Comment

No obvious comments ("Increment counter", "Check if user is null"). No commented-out code. No TODO/FIXME without ticket reference.

## 7. Comment Decision Tree

1. Security/auth check? → `// AUTH:` or `// SECURITY:`
2. Logs to audit tables? → `// AUDIT:`
3. Non-obvious why? → Explanation comment
4. Business rule? → Context/ticket reference
5. Otherwise → Usually no comment

## 8. Pre-Commit Checklist & Grep Commands

See full checklist in this file. Auditors: `rg "// SECURITY:"`, `rg "// AUTH:"`, `rg "// AUDIT:"`, `rg "@security"`, `rg "@audit"` in codebase.
